  "description": "Two expectations on A-601 are in force from Monday: Door 101's at the architect's 100% CD, and Door 102's by Friday 5 June. A-601's only evidence for each is a statement at the still-planned 100% CD, which has no occurrence time. No ending is recorded for either property, and neither is a limitation: on 8 June Door 101's property reads not_yet_due and is upcoming work, Door 102's reads outstanding and overdue, and what remains lists no limitation. When 100% CD is published on 9 June, that write records both end acts at the publication instant, by fulfillment: on time for Door 101 and late for Door 102. The earlier frame still shows Door 102 outstanding.",
  "note": "6.5.5: \"Evidence that has no occurrence time (4.2.4), such as a statement at a milestone that is not yet published, satisfies no instant while it has none. Until then the property's standing is derived without it, `not_yet_due` or `outstanding` by its timing scope (6.2.1), and no ending is recorded for it (7.6.6). Once the milestone's publication gives the evidence an occurrence time, it qualifies under 6.5.1\". 7.6.6: \"An expectation property's ending is never a `no_occurrence_time` limitation\". late_by is computed between the ends of the deadline's interval (the end of 5 June) and the evidence's (09:01 on 9 June), README section 5.",
